      "id": 5,
      "title": "Follow an event across Kafka",
      "type": "text",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Publisher → Kafka → Worker A or Worker B\n\nPublish a fresh order, copy its **traceId**, and open [Jaeger](http://localhost:16686). Expand **kafka:process apm.orders → workflow:KafkaOrderRouting** to inspect its actions.\n\n**[Worker A traces](http://localhost:16686/search?service=worker-a)** · **[Worker B traces](http://localhost:16686/search?service=worker-b)** · **[Publisher traces](http://localhost:16686/search?service=kafka-order-publisher)**\n\nEach record runs on one consumer. Its trace links the publisher to the worker that handled that event.\n\n### Metrics and routing\n\n**[Workflow metrics](http://localhost:3000/d/siglo-live-monitoring)** — duration, throughput, completions, failures, and retries across both workers.\n\n**[Prometheus targets](http://localhost:9090/targets)** — verify the monitor is UP. **[Live monitor](http://127.0.0.1:4400)** — routing graphs and context."
      }
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Kafka routing: what to look for",
      "type": "text",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "| Event | Inspect in the selected worker’s trace |\n|---|---|\n| Standard | `reserveStock → chargePayment → shipOrder`; gift wrapping is skipped |\n| Gift | `reserveStock → chargePayment → wrapGift → shipOrder` |\n| Review | `queueReview`; payment and shipping do not run |\n| Cancellation | `recordCancellation`; the fulfillment route does not run |\n| Unsupported | Failed `rejectUnsupported` and workflow spans; adapter quarantines the record |\n| Invalid JSON | Consumer handling span, with no workflow span; parsing fails before execution |\n| Duplicate event | Consumer handling span, with no new workflow span; PostgreSQL returns the completed claim |\n\n**Continuity across replicas:** the same trace ID follows each published record to its assigned worker. Replaying a completed event can land on either replica without repeating fulfillment. The shared metrics count workflow lifecycle events, including nested flows; they do not identify individual workers or measure Kafka consumer lag."
      }
    }
